 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.civilizaciones.01.mayas-passive",
-  "title": "Voz pasiva y se pasiva en textos históricos",
+  "title": "The passive with ser: what was built and deciphered",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "Historical writing uses two passive constructions almost interchangeably: *ser* + participle (*fue descifrada*), which often names who did the action with *por*, and the *se* passive (*se talló*, *se han identificado*), which drops the doer entirely and reads more naturally when the agent doesn't matter. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the passive with *ser* + past participle from B1 Unit 18: *Tikal fue abandonada*. The thing that receives the action is the subject, and the participle agrees with it in gender and number. History books use this form a lot."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "La escritura maya fue descifrada en gran parte gracias al trabajo del lingüista soviético Yuri Knórozov.",
-          "english": "Maya writing was deciphered largely thanks to the work of Soviet linguist Yuri Knórozov."
+          "spanish": "Las ciudades mayas fueron construidas en medio de la selva.",
+          "english": "The Maya cities were built in the middle of the rainforest."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Durante mucho tiempo se pensó que las ciudades del sur fueron simplemente abandonadas por guerras o mala administración.",
-          "english": "For a long time it was thought that the southern cities were simply abandoned due to wars or poor administration."
+          "spanish": "Los glifos fueron descifrados en el siglo XX.",
+          "english": "The glyphs were deciphered in the twentieth century."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "En Copán se talló la escalinata jeroglífica más larga conocida.",
-          "english": "In Copán, the longest known hieroglyphic stairway was carved."
+          "spanish": "Tikal fue abandonada poco a poco.",
+          "english": "Tikal was abandoned little by little."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Se han identificado más de ochocientos glifos distintos.",
-          "english": "More than eight hundred distinct glyphs have been identified."
+          "spanish": "Los reyes eran enterrados en los templos.",
+          "english": "The kings were buried in the temples."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Reach for *ser* + participle when you want to name who did it (*fue descifrada por Knórozov*); reach for *se* + verb when the doer is unknown, irrelevant, or already obvious from context (*se talló*, *se han identificado*). Both are more common in formal historical writing than in everyday speech."
+      "content": "The participle agrees with the subject: *fue abandonada*, *fueron abandonadas*, *fueron descifrados*. If you name who did it, use *por*: *los glifos fueron descifrados por los especialistas*. The verb *ser* shows the tense: *fue* for a single event, *era* for something repeated."
     }
   ]
