 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.civilizaciones.05.legado-passive",
-  "title": "Voz pasiva para hablar del legado",
+  "title": "Then and now: the imperfect and the present perfect",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "Passive voice fits legacy talk naturally: what matters is what happened to the word, the crop, the language — not who exactly did it. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the *imperfecto* from B1 Unit 5, and the present perfect from A2 Unit 1, for change over time. The imperfect describes how things were before (*antes se hablaban…*, *no podían estudiar*); the present perfect links the past to today (*han creado programas*, *ha crecido*)."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Cientos de palabras fueron tomadas directamente del náhuatl o del quechua.",
