 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.llegadaeuropeos.01.viaje",
-  "title": "Pretérito para narrar hechos históricos",
+  "title": "Cuando and mientras: what happened and what was going on",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The preterite tense is the backbone of historical narration: it presents a chain of completed, one-after-another events (departed, sighted land, landed, died) rather than an ongoing state. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *cuando* and *mientras* from A2 Unit 13. *Mientras* + imperfect gives the background, what was going on during a long stretch of time. *Cuando* + preterite marks a single moment. Together they let you tell the story of a voyage."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Cristóbal Colón partió del puerto de Palos de la Frontera el 3 de agosto de 1492 con tres barcos.",
-          "english": "Christopher Columbus set sail from the port of Palos de la Frontera on August 3, 1492 with three ships."
+          "spanish": "Mientras los barcos cruzaban el Atlántico, los marineros tenían miedo.",
+          "english": "While the ships were crossing the Atlantic, the sailors were afraid."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "El 12 de octubre, un marinero de la Pinta llamado Rodrigo de Triana avistó tierra por primera vez.",
-          "english": "On October 12, a sailor from the Pinta named Rodrigo de Triana sighted land for the first time."
+          "spanish": "Cuando Colón desembarcó, tomó posesión de la isla.",
+          "english": "When Columbus landed, he took possession of the island."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Colón murió en 1506 sin admitir jamás que no había llegado a Asia.",
-          "english": "Columbus died in 1506 never admitting that he hadn't reached Asia."
+          "spanish": "Mientras Colón exploraba las islas, buscaba oro.",
+          "english": "While Columbus was exploring the islands, he was looking for gold."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "En 1507, un cartógrafo alemán llamado Martin Waldseemüller publicó un mapa que bautizó el nuevo continente.",
-          "english": "In 1507, a German cartographer named Martin Waldseemüller published a map that named the new continent."
+          "spanish": "Cuando los barcos llegaron a la isla, la tripulación llevaba semanas en el mar.",
+          "english": "When the ships reached the island, the crew had been at sea for weeks."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Reach for the preterite (*partió, avistó, murió, publicó*) whenever a historical text moves the story forward one finished event at a time. Save the imperfect for description or background that was ongoing at the time (*la tripulación estaba nerviosa*) — most history-book sentences lean heavily preterite."
+      "content": "*Mientras* is followed by the imperfect when you describe two things going on together (*mientras cruzaban… tenían miedo*). *Cuando* is followed by the preterite for the event that interrupts or follows (*cuando desembarcó, tomó posesión*). Both words are written without an accent in these uses."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-llegadaeuropeos-02-encuentro-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-llegadaeuropeos-02-encuentro-gr.json
