 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.llegadaeuropeos.04.nuevos-mundos",
-  "title": "Expresar causa y consecuencia",
+  "title": "Debido a and a raíz de: giving causes",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*Debido a que* and *ya que* introduce a cause before or after the main clause; *por eso* and *como resultado de* introduce a consequence, usually at the start of a new sentence. Historical writing leans on all four to explain why something happened, not just that it did. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know formal cause connectors like *debido a* and *a raíz de* from B1 Unit 6. *Debido a* + noun gives the cause; *debido a que* + verb does the same with a whole clause. *A raíz de* points to an event that started a change."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Debido a que la población indígena del Caribe ya se había reducido drásticamente, los colonos recurrieron al tráfico de personas esclavizadas desde África.",
-          "english": "Because the indigenous population of the Caribbean had already declined drastically, colonists increasingly turned to trafficking enslaved people from Africa."
+          "spanish": "Debido a las epidemias, murió una gran parte de la población.",
+          "english": "Because of the epidemics, a large part of the population died."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Por eso, muchos historiadores consideran la caña de azúcar uno de los motores principales detrás del comercio transatlántico de esclavos.",
-          "english": "That's why many historians consider sugarcane one of the main engines behind the transatlantic slave trade."
+          "spanish": "A raíz de la llegada del caballo, algunos pueblos cambiaron su forma de cazar.",
+          "english": "As a result of the arrival of the horse, some peoples changed the way they hunted."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "La población indígena no tenía ninguna inmunidad, ya que estos patógenos habían evolucionado junto a los animales domesticados de Eurasia.",
-          "english": "The indigenous population had no immunity, since these pathogens had evolved alongside Eurasia's domesticated animals."
+          "spanish": "Debido a que la papa crecía bien en climas fríos, se hizo importante en Europa.",
+          "english": "Because the potato grew well in cold climates, it became important in Europe."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Como resultado de esta catástrofe demográfica, millones de hectáreas de tierras de cultivo volvieron a cubrirse de bosque.",
-          "english": "As a result of this demographic catastrophe, millions of hectares of farmland became forest again."
+          "spanish": "A raíz de las epidemias, muchos pueblos perdieron a gran parte de su gente.",
+          "english": "As a result of the epidemics, many peoples lost a large part of their people."
